WEBVTT

00:00.810 --> 00:03.130
The unchanging course of the stars...

00:03.780 --> 00:05.930
You lied to me, asshole!

00:05.930 --> 00:07.660
The doings of mankind...

00:06.910 --> 00:08.720
Look over there! The Solar Knights!

00:08.720 --> 00:10.220
Wait, shithead!

00:10.890 --> 00:12.980
The dust, gathering on the windowsill...

00:14.400 --> 00:15.850
A bard!

00:17.900 --> 00:19.750
The sigh of a man with strange loves...

00:21.870 --> 00:23.990
The shriveled-up body of
a Black Greatrock Worm.

00:24.380 --> 00:27.530
Decorations brought back from
the Valley of Dragons...

00:28.400 --> 00:34.130
The half-eaten food of an adventurer who fled
the Labyrinth and now sobs through his meal...

00:30.480 --> 00:32.790
What the hell were you
thinking, you bastard?

00:34.610 --> 00:37.800
It's all so beautiful!

00:38.490 --> 00:40.630
He's like a poet.

00:40.630 --> 00:42.500
Has he been like that the whole time?

00:42.500 --> 00:44.210
Yup.

00:44.210 --> 00:45.520
If anything, he's calmer than usual.

00:48.050 --> 00:51.810
A high-quality igniter,
modified to one's tastes and much loved!

01:00.000 --> 01:03.670
I can feel the history it carries.

01:03.670 --> 01:04.720
Thanks.

01:05.340 --> 01:07.880
That thing you've got there
looks good on you, too.

01:09.040 --> 01:10.680
Right? Right?

01:15.190 --> 01:17.250
You look wonderful.

01:17.250 --> 01:19.620
That's right!
It looks impressive, even if you don't!

01:20.010 --> 01:22.670
Curran, that's not a compliment.

01:23.670 --> 01:27.570
Kizuna, how many times do you have to hear
it from all of us before you're satisfied?

01:28.060 --> 01:30.480
There's no such thing as
too many compliments.

01:30.480 --> 01:33.500
They're something both the
giver and receiver can enjoy.

01:34.520 --> 01:35.850
True.

01:35.850 --> 01:37.190
You look great.

01:38.040 --> 01:39.940
Now, let's get to it.

01:40.440 --> 01:41.820
First, Curran.

01:42.400 --> 01:43.710
Zem.

01:44.220 --> 01:45.320
Tiana.

01:45.740 --> 01:50.280
I'd like to entrust you with the
task of keeping our funds safe.

01:52.410 --> 01:54.970
It seems to be protected with magic.

01:55.270 --> 01:59.590
And this is a magic abacus. It can calculate
automatically, which is a great help.

01:59.970 --> 02:04.980
And this is what I'd like
you all to protect.

02:06.400 --> 02:10.050
Two bronze pieces.
Three small bronze pieces.

02:10.050 --> 02:12.460
230 dinah all together.

02:12.460 --> 02:13.860
What about it?

02:13.860 --> 02:15.350
You could buy a snack.

02:16.250 --> 02:18.990
This is all the wealth the
Survivors have right now.

02:21.090 --> 02:22.510
W-Wait.

02:22.510 --> 02:23.890
What does that mean?

02:23.890 --> 02:26.140
Did we overspend a little?

02:25.380 --> 02:27.740
A snack is all you could buy!

02:28.040 --> 02:31.340
So... let's go make some money, guys!

02:31.340 --> 02:33.000
Yeah!

02:33.000 --> 02:44.810
Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World

04:03.760 --> 04:08.680
"A Meeting with the Iron Tigers."

04:13.380 --> 04:14.880
Tiana,

04:16.490 --> 04:20.300
as of today, you're no longer
a student at this school.

04:21.140 --> 04:22.050
Yes...

04:23.060 --> 04:25.700
But you're still a mage.

04:29.000 --> 04:33.900
Oh, you may have this as a gift.

04:35.710 --> 04:38.330
An igniter?

04:38.330 --> 04:39.950
It's a goodbye gift.

04:41.200 --> 04:43.450
You'd wanted it, right?

04:46.220 --> 04:47.980
Thank you, sir.

04:48.780 --> 04:53.250
I'd ruined the career of somebody I admired.

04:53.820 --> 04:55.720
He'd been caught up in the scandal with me.

04:56.230 --> 05:01.010
I'd taken away the title of Sage
that he'd wanted so badly.

05:01.800 --> 05:02.850
Forever.

05:03.890 --> 05:07.580
But still, he spoke like nothing bothered
him at all, and this is what he said.

05:07.580 --> 05:13.380
"Because nobody needs us, we are free."

05:14.690 --> 05:18.170
But freedom can be quite restrictive.

05:18.170 --> 05:19.000
Huh?

05:19.800 --> 05:21.240
No, nothing.

05:23.670 --> 05:30.150
And we're going to find ourselves
restricted in many ways.

05:30.500 --> 05:36.010
We want to be free, but we
want somebody to need us.

05:36.560 --> 05:43.660
Perhaps humans deserve to be destroyed.

05:45.960 --> 05:47.160
I'm joking.

05:51.370 --> 05:53.340
It's strange, don't you think?

05:53.660 --> 05:57.970
Even after all this, we can still laugh.

05:58.800 --> 06:05.220
Perhaps it's a sign that
the worst is yet to come.

06:06.080 --> 06:11.530
I was never able tell if you're
joking or not, Master.

06:11.530 --> 06:14.210
W-Was it not funny?

06:14.960 --> 06:16.610
It's more like...

06:18.730 --> 06:20.050
It's inappropriate.

06:23.260 --> 06:25.310
I see.

06:28.400 --> 06:31.950
Inappropriate? I suppose you're right.

06:31.950 --> 06:34.100
I suppose you may be right.

06:36.630 --> 06:41.740
You seem to be enjoying this somehow.

06:44.730 --> 06:47.310
Master, you're laughing too much.

06:47.310 --> 06:48.850
I'm sorry.

06:49.800 --> 06:52.480
Just, whenever there's a silence,
I can't help myself...

06:55.640 --> 06:59.350
I say whatever's on my mind.

07:01.490 --> 07:05.300
Um, I'll be going.

07:05.300 --> 07:08.000
Oh, yes.

07:11.560 --> 07:14.860
Was there something I could do for him?

07:15.290 --> 07:19.090
I wondered that, even though I knew
I was overstepping myself.

07:19.090 --> 07:21.660
It was rude, almost impudent.

07:23.930 --> 07:26.650
I'm sorry. This is all my fault.

07:28.780 --> 07:30.760
This is goodbye, isn't it?

07:30.760 --> 07:32.130
Yes, of course it is.

07:35.080 --> 07:38.340
I'll give you one last lesson, then.

07:41.140 --> 07:44.800
To know who you are.

07:44.800 --> 07:49.500
To know what you've learned,
what you can do...

07:49.500 --> 07:52.780
That's a treasure that
nobody can take from you.

07:52.780 --> 07:55.200
Remember that, at all times.

08:00.590 --> 08:04.810
That's not a joke, is it?

08:07.610 --> 08:08.820
I'm sorry.

08:09.530 --> 08:11.680
I couldn't say.

08:17.140 --> 08:21.750
Am I the only who sometimes wonders
when I wake up in the morning

08:22.390 --> 08:25.550
if maybe I'll open my eyes and everything
will be back to how it was,

08:25.880 --> 08:29.030
before all this happened?

08:36.160 --> 08:38.720
If only it were true...

08:39.490 --> 08:42.530
I wonder if I'll wake up
in my bed in the mansion,

08:42.530 --> 08:44.990
surrounded by pillows and fluffy blankets,

08:44.990 --> 08:50.920
and wonder how many wonderful things
I'll learn about Alex today,

08:50.920 --> 08:53.400
or how many times I'll
be of use to my Master.

08:53.990 --> 08:59.950
I was so happy, so blessed,
to be a dreaming maiden like that.

09:01.540 --> 09:05.120
I'm sure everybody else has had
the same thought at least once.

09:06.030 --> 09:10.640
"If only I could go back in time
to when everything was fine..."

09:19.730 --> 09:25.330
We dream of a wish that not even the most
ancient, powerful magic could grant,

09:27.260 --> 09:32.690
again and again, before we wake up...

09:34.010 --> 09:35.530
Your birthday present.

09:35.880 --> 09:39.130
Wow, you remembered!

09:39.130 --> 09:41.460
This is just what I wanted!

09:41.460 --> 09:44.350
I'm glad you like it, Claudine.

09:44.350 --> 09:45.390
But...

09:46.290 --> 09:49.780
More! I want more!

09:51.500 --> 09:54.940
The shriveled-up body of a Black
Greatrock Worm, the half-eaten food...

09:54.940 --> 09:58.000
I want more!

09:56.750 --> 09:58.400
C-Claudine?

09:58.910 --> 10:04.370
Everything that changed since I was sealed
away, everything that hasn't changed...

10:04.370 --> 10:07.700
I want to see it all!

10:06.270 --> 10:09.660
Get a hold of yourself, Claudine!

10:14.800 --> 10:17.210
Was that his telepathy?

10:18.370 --> 10:22.110
Don't send your sleep talk into my brain.

10:22.110 --> 10:25.950
I want to see it all... to know it all...

10:27.750 --> 10:29.400
Is it just me?

10:31.140 --> 10:32.950
Is it just me?

10:34.460 --> 10:36.430
Is it just me?

10:38.410 --> 10:39.520
Good morning.

10:39.840 --> 10:41.470
Morning!

10:41.820 --> 10:44.200
I have no past I want to return to!

10:44.200 --> 10:46.690
The time I'm spending with you now
is the most fun I've ever had!

10:46.690 --> 10:48.590
How innocent...

10:48.590 --> 10:51.100
I can't look!
I can't bear to look at him, Nick!

10:51.100 --> 10:52.830
I wish I was like that.

11:05.190 --> 11:07.850
Yup, that's a Rasetsu Ogre.

11:07.850 --> 11:09.720
I thought we beat him before...

11:09.720 --> 11:13.090
It's not the same one, actually.

11:13.340 --> 11:16.610
They're reborn each time
the Miasma gets thick.

11:16.610 --> 11:18.360
Poor things.

11:18.360 --> 11:20.860
It's fun to chat with everybody.

11:20.860 --> 11:25.270
Telepathy's not for chatting and having fun.

11:25.270 --> 11:29.070
I'm nervous. I've never even
used a Communications Gem.

11:30.010 --> 11:32.800
I can hear you from all the way over here!

11:33.120 --> 11:35.890
You're too far ahead!

11:35.890 --> 11:38.500
My true power isn't telepathy!

11:38.500 --> 11:41.390
Behold the power of my blade!

11:42.380 --> 11:45.400
Idiot! What was the point
of using telepathy, then?!

11:50.140 --> 11:53.640
A brute-force attack won't work on me!

12:05.760 --> 12:07.040
Parallel.

12:08.410 --> 12:09.800
There's more of them!

12:09.800 --> 12:11.310
He did something!

12:11.310 --> 12:12.640
That's not fair.

12:13.240 --> 12:16.640
I can use my telepathy to hear you all!

12:20.810 --> 12:23.890
I can create up to five copies.

12:23.890 --> 12:26.430
I feel tired for some reason.

12:26.430 --> 12:31.350
Of course. I'm using your
stamina and magic to do it.

12:31.350 --> 12:32.430
What?

12:32.430 --> 12:35.260
Haha! Don't worry about it.

12:35.260 --> 12:36.430
Delete!

12:39.630 --> 12:42.780
Well, I feel like I should be more
concerned about part of that.

12:42.780 --> 12:44.820
But I'm honestly amazed.

12:44.820 --> 12:46.150
Your Parallel skill is amazing,

12:46.150 --> 12:48.190
but so is your skill with a sword.

12:48.510 --> 12:52.350
Sword skills were installed in me
during the development stage.

12:53.450 --> 12:55.450
Installed?

12:55.450 --> 13:00.050
I mean that I absorbed the techniques
of a swordsman who used me in the past!

13:00.050 --> 13:01.460
I knew it! That's cheating!

13:01.460 --> 13:04.990
It's not cheating! How rude.

13:04.990 --> 13:07.910
Either way, we're definitely
glad to have you along.

13:07.910 --> 13:10.460
I've got my most powerful technique, too.

13:10.460 --> 13:13.350
I'm not planning on using
Union at all for a while.

13:13.350 --> 13:15.410
Wh-Why?

13:15.410 --> 13:19.120
We can't use something that makes us
collapse from exhaustion afterward.

13:19.120 --> 13:20.970
What? Stingy bastard.

13:20.970 --> 13:23.730
It's good to have something
we can rely on if we have to.

13:23.730 --> 13:26.240
Yup. We're counting on you.

13:26.240 --> 13:27.990
I'm hungry!

13:27.990 --> 13:29.650
Maybe we should get something to eat.

13:29.650 --> 13:30.990
What about you two?

13:30.990 --> 13:32.610
I'm hungry!

13:32.610 --> 13:35.370
I'll go check on the dragons, then...

13:35.370 --> 13:38.490
I'll go check on the ladies, then.

13:38.490 --> 13:41.980
Hey! Don't use telepathy for chit-chat!

13:46.990 --> 13:49.120
So you did end up coming with us.

13:49.850 --> 13:52.140
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

13:51.620 --> 13:53.840
No fair using mental attacks!

13:54.120 --> 13:58.220
I'm in my "fun" phase, and I have
fun no matter what I'm doing.

13:58.800 --> 14:01.220
What if somebody drops a pair
of chopsticks? Is that fun?

14:02.290 --> 14:05.100
It might be!

14:06.260 --> 14:08.590
What are you talking about?

14:09.580 --> 14:11.500
I smell something good!

14:13.480 --> 14:14.130
This is...

14:15.220 --> 14:19.060
I want more!

14:19.060 --> 14:21.480
It stimulates the appetite.

14:21.480 --> 14:23.540
No, wait...

14:25.020 --> 14:27.190
Well, whatever.

14:28.530 --> 14:31.730
Yeah, this is good.

14:31.730 --> 14:35.520
If you're not careful with how you
prepare the fish, it gets all dry.

14:35.520 --> 14:39.190
But they make it just right,
and the sauce is great, too!

14:39.190 --> 14:42.050
They know how to cook!

14:42.050 --> 14:44.670
You've got high expectations.

14:44.670 --> 14:46.890
I am a foodie, after all.

14:46.890 --> 14:49.580
Yeah, you do eat through our food budget.

14:50.410 --> 14:53.400
Survivors Rule #1.

14:54.200 --> 14:56.070
Sorry, sorry.

14:57.310 --> 15:00.650
I'm so happy you remembered!

15:06.280 --> 15:09.900
That's Claudine...

15:09.900 --> 15:12.750
This is just what I wanted!

15:12.750 --> 15:15.810
I'm glad you like it, Claudine.

15:17.080 --> 15:20.000
I'm glad you like it, Claudine.

15:22.110 --> 15:25.830
Actually, I have to go back to my hometown.

15:26.870 --> 15:30.480
My mom's sick and doesn't
have much time left.

15:30.480 --> 15:31.660
What?

15:33.010 --> 15:35.410
But it's so far away.

15:35.410 --> 15:38.170
It's a month by carriage!

15:38.480 --> 15:41.830
I need so much money!

15:41.830 --> 15:46.480
Money! I want money so badly!

15:46.480 --> 15:48.160
Sob! Sob! Sob!

15:48.800 --> 15:50.970
Poor Claudine!

15:50.970 --> 15:53.740
Don't worry. I'll take care of it all.

15:53.070 --> 15:54.170
Hey there.

15:56.370 --> 15:57.200
Nick!

15:57.200 --> 15:58.930
Wh-Who are you?

15:59.240 --> 16:04.190
Poor thing. Your mom moved away, huh?

16:04.190 --> 16:06.990
You told me she lived
three days to the East.

16:07.940 --> 16:10.450
Th-Three days is pretty far!

16:11.320 --> 16:13.400
Oh, and happy birthday.

16:13.400 --> 16:16.700
You know, you're the first person I've met
who has two birthdays in a year!

16:18.270 --> 16:20.470
Wh-Who is this, Claudine?

16:20.470 --> 16:23.590
I-I don't remember inviting you.

16:24.200 --> 16:26.080
Wh-What?

16:26.390 --> 16:30.080
If you sell that thing,
it's an easy fraud charge.

16:30.080 --> 16:33.240
It's an expensive luxury item,
and clearly appraised.

16:35.900 --> 16:38.340
Let's go. Looks like this
weirdo wants to bother us.

16:38.340 --> 16:41.350
So, what's next? You're going to live the
rest of your life with a bounty on your head?

16:41.790 --> 16:43.890
Your mom will be so sad.

16:46.160 --> 16:46.970
Damn it!

16:47.920 --> 16:51.360
Damage it, and you're liable for damages.

16:55.850 --> 16:58.030
Here, this is yours, right?

17:01.790 --> 17:04.630
Was she lying to me?

17:05.450 --> 17:06.820
Hey, Nick.

17:08.090 --> 17:10.550
Your meal's gotten cold.

17:10.550 --> 17:12.090
Oh, sorry.

17:12.090 --> 17:15.880
I'll take another Alley Cat Pudding
Parfait with extra caramel!

17:17.440 --> 17:22.630
Most gathering quests involve plants
which only bloom in the Labyrinths.

17:22.630 --> 17:24.150
Herbs, poisons...

17:24.150 --> 17:26.730
Zem would know more about that than me.

17:26.730 --> 17:30.680
If it's a cave Labyrinth,
they'll ask for ores and jewels.

17:31.020 --> 17:34.860
That's more suited for a dwarf who
grew up in the mountains than us.

17:40.330 --> 17:42.850
Did you get to see your mom, Claudine?

17:42.850 --> 17:46.400
This is a present from Mom.
She said to say hello.

17:46.730 --> 17:48.730
Glad to hear she's doing well.

17:48.730 --> 17:51.070
She's made a full recovery, actually!

17:51.070 --> 17:52.560
Amazing.

17:52.560 --> 17:55.440
I'd love to recruit her for the Survivors.

17:56.580 --> 18:00.560
You weren't very nice to our
Claudine here, yesterday.

18:00.560 --> 18:01.940
"Our"?

18:01.940 --> 18:06.150
Oh, I just told her not to make her mom sad.

18:06.910 --> 18:09.050
So, you're with the Iron Kitties?

18:08.490 --> 18:09.550
The Iron Tigers!

18:10.680 --> 18:12.030
Leon.

18:12.030 --> 18:15.490
Sorry. I'm bad with names.

18:16.000 --> 18:18.150
You were planning on selling the necklace

18:18.150 --> 18:20.710
to get the funds to run from
the Iron Tigers, right?

18:20.710 --> 18:21.700
What?

18:21.700 --> 18:23.450
L-Lies!

18:23.730 --> 18:26.320
He's just mad because I dumped him!

18:26.320 --> 18:29.450
If girls don't like you,
you see every girl as a villain.

18:29.450 --> 18:31.950
And you villains both get along, then?

18:31.950 --> 18:34.200
Why don't we take this outside, asshole?

18:35.890 --> 18:37.200
Hey, Nick!

18:37.200 --> 18:40.530
The kitty wants to sunbathe, he says.

18:43.630 --> 18:45.300
This'll do, I suppose.

18:45.300 --> 18:47.480
Yeah. Lots of sunlight.

18:51.960 --> 18:53.430
I'm sorry!

18:54.050 --> 18:56.850
Man, I am so sorry!

18:58.390 --> 19:01.240
Claudine underestimated
what you were capable of.

19:01.540 --> 19:04.830
It's not easy to make money in a party.

19:05.530 --> 19:07.540
I've heard all about you guys, you know.

19:08.280 --> 19:12.580
And I'm glad you put a stop
to Claudine's bullshit.

19:12.910 --> 19:16.930
As for her... you can have her.

19:17.590 --> 19:22.060
She's conned a lot of people,
and made a lot of enemies.

19:22.060 --> 19:23.690
Like you, right?

19:25.310 --> 19:29.720
She made us a lot of money, but I
think our time together's at an end.

19:29.970 --> 19:31.600
And...

19:32.600 --> 19:38.390
The Dragonian lady, the noble girl,
and that naive-looking priest...

19:38.390 --> 19:41.240
You've even got a kid with you lately.

19:42.160 --> 19:43.220
Well?

19:43.810 --> 19:45.550
You making bank?

19:45.550 --> 19:47.280
What are you talking about?

19:47.280 --> 19:50.640
You're robbing them blind, aren't you?

19:50.640 --> 19:52.260
Like us.

19:52.260 --> 19:53.330
Me?

19:53.730 --> 19:55.680
Robbing Curran or Tiana?

19:57.370 --> 19:58.370
Yeah?

19:59.130 --> 20:00.700
I see...

20:03.050 --> 20:04.210
Right?

20:06.550 --> 20:08.670
Man, I can't believe you...

20:11.350 --> 20:15.760
So, yeah, when you finally
decide to blow up the party

20:15.760 --> 20:17.810
and run off with the money,
let us in on it...

20:20.680 --> 20:23.440
Sorry.

20:23.440 --> 20:26.470
I thought you were a
Tigerian when I hit you.

20:26.470 --> 20:29.780
I don't like hurting wimpy little kitties.

20:37.350 --> 20:38.490
You're good.

20:39.010 --> 20:41.040
You aren't, really.

20:41.040 --> 20:42.510
Sh-Shut up!

20:44.270 --> 20:46.210
I want money, too, you know.

20:47.360 --> 20:50.080
Especially if I don't have to work for it.

20:50.080 --> 20:55.280
But what would the money I got
from scamming them be worth?

20:55.570 --> 21:00.400
Even if I made a fortune,
would the ale I got with it taste good?

21:01.840 --> 21:05.880
Have you gotten to the point where
you can get drunk on ale like that?

21:06.900 --> 21:08.220
Wind Cluster!

21:10.670 --> 21:12.790
I made it in time, little kitty.

21:13.220 --> 21:15.810
If you were listening,
you should have helped earlier.

21:15.810 --> 21:19.010
If you think it's okay to
ambush somebody two on one,

21:19.010 --> 21:20.790
you haven't learned your manners.

21:21.550 --> 21:24.040
It's your fault for eating
a surprise attack—

21:26.730 --> 21:29.420
It's whose fault for eating what now?

21:31.320 --> 21:33.700
The only thing worth eating is food.

21:33.700 --> 21:35.400
Sorry. Thanks for coming.

21:35.930 --> 21:37.050
That's enough!

21:37.660 --> 21:39.060
The old lady!

21:39.370 --> 21:40.820
Call me Vilma!

21:41.150 --> 21:41.960
Ow!

21:41.960 --> 21:43.680
You can't dodge that?

21:44.100 --> 21:45.890
Leon, was it?

21:45.890 --> 21:47.200
That goes for you, too.

21:48.950 --> 21:52.240
Oh, and Curran, let the kid go.

21:56.780 --> 21:58.990
So, what now?

21:58.990 --> 22:01.580
Huh? You didn't come to stop us?

